# ✓ seeded arrivals start with Marta and place Lotte late in the night
# ✓ later nights include a simultaneous pair so the second tap has a real use
# ✓ guest budgets include both price-sensitive and premium customers across seeds
# ✓ ordinary fractional ticks remain valid through a complete unattended night
# ✓ one deterministic nightly dilemma freezes service and time until a valid choice
# ✓ a dilemma freezes an already-reserved pour and consumes only remaining stock
# ✓ landlord comp consumes a real cup and reduces rent; refusal adds a service fee
# ✓ influencer samples consume exactly two cups and change only the next three future budgets
# ✓ inspector paperwork buys patience while tasting honestly increases the nightly rent
# ✓ nightly event saves reject wrong event identities, choices, and rent adjustments
# ✓ pour reserves exactly one cup, keeps batch quality, and rejects duplicate or invalid prices
# ✓ wrong beer, unaffordable prices, and early pours do not satisfy customers
# ✓ tick validates its bound, expires customers, and spills overfilled pours without refunds
# ✓ water is a free fallback and closing settles unresolved customers once with rent
# ✓ closing during a pour consumes its cup and sold-out stock cannot be reserved
# ✓ a promised stout rewards Lotte and gives music next night; skipping her breaks the promise
# ✓ all upgrades apply a real tradeoff while moving to the next preparation day
